markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Color Bank

Each of the following colors align with Code.org branding. Use them in accordance with the breakdown on the previous page.

**Note**: The text color (black or white) on top of the colored circles below represents the text color that should be overlaid on the brand color. These pairings pass WCAG contrast standards.

## Neutrals

These colors should comprise at least 60% of the page, which is achieved through Level Builder's background.

<div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:20px;margin:20px auto;font-size:14pt;">

  <div style="width:180px;border:1px solid #000000;border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;">
    <div style="background:#FFFFFF;height:140px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;">
      <span style="font-size:96px;font-weight:bold;line-height:1;color:#000000;">a</span>
    </div>
    <div style="padding:12px;text-align:center;">
      <div style="font-weight:bold;">White</div>
      <div style="font-size:12pt;">#FFFFFF</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="width:180px;border:1px solid #000000;border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;">
    <div style="background:#000000;height:140px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;">
      <span style="font-size:96px;font-weight:bold;line-height:1;color:#FFFFFF;">a</span>
    </div>
    <div style="padding:12px;text-align:center;">
      <div style="font-weight:bold;">Black</div>
      <div style="font-size:12pt;">#000000</div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

## Primary

Primary brand color. Should be dominant throughout Code.org branding.

<div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:20px;margin:20px auto;font-size:14pt;">

  <div style="width:180px;border:1px solid #000000;border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;">
    <div style="background:#E4E2F8;height:140px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;">
